# Product templates → Cursor delivery

When implementing tasks exported from ASF Planner:

1. Lock product type to one of: `website` | `telegram_bot` | `rest_service` | `ai_automation`
2. Read `templates/<product_type>.md` before coding — Typical MVP is the ceiling
3. Stay inside the template checklist; escalate out-of-scope items (do not invent SaaS / payments / multi-agent)
4. Prefer small, testable slices matching exported task acceptance criteria
5. Reference requirement IDs from the export; do not silently expand scope
6. On blocking product forks → stop (`HumanDecisionRequired`), do not guess

## Per-type anchors

| Type | Template | MVP shape |
|------|----------|-----------|
| website | `templates/website.md` | Brochure/landing, CTA, contact |
| telegram_bot | `templates/telegram_bot.md` | Commands/flow, light state |
| rest_service | `templates/rest_service.md` | Small API, one resource, simple auth |
| ai_automation | `templates/ai_automation.md` | Trigger → step → side effect + logs |

## Export handoff

- Markdown: `GET /projects/{id}/export/tasks?format=markdown`
- JSON: `GET /projects/{id}/export/tasks?format=json`
- Platform rules still apply: `AGENTS.md`, `.cursor/rules/asf.mdc`
